From 0c0c6aae3d93a9cd70092ea55bae0ff7e701d3b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tintu Thomas <tintu.thomas@arm.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Nov 2024 17:41:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] module/cmn_cyprus: Add compact HN table support

Compact HN table is a feature to reduce the usage of target ID table
registers. When enabled, the driver doesn't need to program target HN-S IDs
for remote hashed regions. Apart from that, there are a set of new registers
specifically added to control the region configuration with compact HN table.

This change checks whether Compact HN table is enabled in the mesh and
if enabled the driver skips programming target IDs for remote regions.
Also, add compact CPAG controls and compact hash controls for per chip NUMA
config as follows. For per chip NUMA, CPAG hash bits are programmed with
hardcoded zeros to always point to the first element(CPAG0) in the CPAG table.
HN-S hash bits are all in passthrough mode. Finally, program the CPAG ID and
enable CPA for CPAG0.

Signed-off-by: Tintu Thomas <tintu.thomas@arm.com>
Change-Id: I74230f316044e4922aea732f34da37d136c6d3d2

Signed-off-by: Jon Mason <jon.mason@arm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
